{
  "faulty_agent": "Assistant",
  "faulty_step": 6,
  "reason": "The assistant incorrectly reported 11 available T-shirt options, but only 10 variants in the product details have available=true. This wrong count was never corrected and caused the task to fail."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "Assistant",
  "faulty_step": 30,
  "reason": "The assistant failed to disclose that cancel_pending_order would cancel the entire pending order, not just the hose, and obtained confirmation only for the hose. If it had correctly listed the full-order cancellation and asked for confirmation, the user would likely have declined, preventing the incorrect $1619.34 refund and final total."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "Assistant",
  "faulty_step": 28,
  "reason": "The assistant incorrectly treated order #W5481803 as a boot-only order and said only the $253.54 boot would be refunded, ignoring that the same pending order also contained the kettle. This misrepresentation led the user to confirm a cancellation that canceled the entire order, violating the instruction to keep the kettle if the boot could not be canceled separately."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "Assistant",
  "faulty_step": 8,
  "reason": "The assistant looked up the wrong order, #W7449508, which contained an espresso machine and sneakers rather than the tablet. This caused it to give the incorrect tracking number in step 10."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "Assistant",
  "faulty_step": 16,
  "reason": "The assistant incorrectly claimed it could not get the new address from order details and did not retrieve the order, so it never obtained the address needed to complete the update."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "Assistant",
  "faulty_step": 16,
  "reason": "The assistant modified the order items before updating the address, which changed the order status to 'pending (item modified)' and made the address modification impossible. It should have updated the address first while the order was still pending."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "Assistant",
  "faulty_step": 26,
  "reason": "The assistant cancelled a pending order without first listing the action details and obtaining the user's explicit confirmation, including the required cancellation reason. This is the earliest decisive policy violation in the consequential-action flow."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "User",
  "faulty_step": 31,
  "reason": "The user rejected the only policy-compliant way to get the cheaper speaker into the pending order (replacing the existing speaker) and instead insisted on adding a new item. This led to no order modification and the final total remained the original order total."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "Assistant",
  "faulty_step": 24,
  "reason": "The assistant had sufficient explicit confirmation to perform the exchange but did not invoke the exchange tool; instead it stalled with an email explanation and another confirmation request, so the exchange was never executed."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "Assistant",
  "faulty_step": 14,
  "reason": "The assistant prematurely concluded there were only two pending orders without checking order #W6832752, which was also pending. This caused it to omit that order from the address updates later."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "Assistant",
  "faulty_step": 20,
  "reason": "The assistant modified the pending order's item before updating its address, which changed the status to 'pending (item modified)' and made the address update impossible. It should have updated the address first, or at least not performed the irreversible item modification before completing the address request."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "Orchestrator",
  "faulty_step": 9,
  "reason": "The Orchestrator selected 'The Tenant' for availability despite the IMDb result showing a 2h 6m runtime, violating the less-than-2-hours constraint. Correctly excluding it and asking for the next qualifying films would have avoided the invalid final answer."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "Orchestrator",
  "faulty_step": 5,
  "reason": "The Orchestrator accepted the $1.08 billion sale of 1800 Owens Street as the answer, but that was a building/property sale, not a high-rise apartment unit sale. It should have continued searching for an actual apartment sale before marking the request satisfied."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "WebSurfer",
  "faulty_step": 12,
  "reason": "WebSurfer was asked to scan the video but instead scrolled the page into comments, so it never captured frames or timestamps; this uncorrected failure caused the repeated loop and later crash."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "Orchestrator",
  "faulty_step": 3,
  "reason": "The task required using Google Finance, but the Orchestrator's first instruction to WebSurfer allowed 'another credible financial resource' instead of requiring Google Finance, so the team never checked the specified source and looped on other sites. If step 3 had directed WebSurfer to Google Finance, the answer could have been found within the round limit."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "Orchestrator",
  "faulty_step": 36,
  "reason": "The Orchestrator's ledger-update model call failed with an OpenAI API connection error while processing WebSurfer's final message at step 36, aborting the run. Had that model call succeeded, the run would most likely have finalized normally."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "WebSurfer",
  "faulty_step": 16,
  "reason": "WebSurfer only applied the 2+ bedroom filter, leaving the bathroom filter at 0+, and did not apply the required 2+ bathroom constraint before the run ended."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "WebSurfer",
  "faulty_step": 24,
  "reason": "WebSurfer was explicitly instructed to search the article for keywords to locate the paper link, but it only scrolled one page and did not find or open the link, so the system never reached the paper and the run stalled/crashed."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "Orchestrator",
  "faulty_step": 9,
  "reason": "The Orchestrator accepted unverified Bing search results as a confirmed list of supermarkets within 2 blocks and selected Trader Joe's and Whole Foods without checking their addresses against the 2-block constraint. This committed the run to an incorrect candidate set, leading to the wrong final answer."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "Orchestrator",
  "faulty_step": 2,
  "reason": "The Orchestrator's first ledger decision assigned FileSurfer to 'listen' to the MP3, ignoring the available ComputerTerminal for local transcription. This wrong delegation set the run into repeated failed listening/upload loops instead of transcribing the audio."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "FileSurfer",
  "faulty_step": 16,
  "reason": "FileSurfer fabricated a local 'Download complete' file at a placeholder path instead of actually opening the book, and then kept returning that same page, so the system never accessed page 11. Had it correctly opened/extracted the file (or reported that no local file existed), the run could have proceeded to the answer."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "WebSurfer",
  "faulty_step": 8,
  "reason": "WebSurfer used a generic Bing search instead of a proper map/radius search and reported only a partial, unfiltered list of gyms, causing the system to miss other West Virginia gyms within 5 miles of the Mothman Museum."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "Orchestrator",
  "faulty_step": 33,
  "reason": "After WebSurfer reported a successful local download path, the Orchestrator's instruction to FileSurfer omitted that path, causing FileSurfer to guess an incorrect file location and fail to extract the volume. Including the known path would most likely have let FileSurfer search the correct PDF and succeed."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "Orchestrator",
  "faulty_step": 17,
  "reason": "After the dojos.info list showed the nearest schools were over 1.4 miles away, the Orchestrator should have abandoned that list and searched specifically within a five-minute walk of 11 Wall St. Instead it marked progress and sent WebSurfer to click Details/Contact on irrelevant schools, causing the loop and wrong final answer."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "Orchestrator",
  "faulty_step": 61,
  "reason": "The Orchestrator accepted an unfiltered 'near' search result as if the listed restaurants were within 1 block of Washington Square Park and moved on to menu checks without verifying addresses, dine-in status, or vegan prices. This uncorrected assumption led directly to the wrong final candidates."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "WebSurfer",
  "faulty_step": 97,
  "reason": "WebSurfer opened the oldest headstone (Dastardly Mash) but only transcribed Dastardly's own epitaph instead of identifying and reading the headstone visible in the background. This uncorrected omission caused the run to loop and hit the round limit."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "Orchestrator",
  "faulty_step": 37,
  "reason": "After correctly planning to open Ted Danson's IMDb profile in step 36, the Orchestrator incorrectly declared a stall and replanned, abandoning that efficient path and restarting broad searches that led to repeated scrolling and failure."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "Orchestrator",
  "faulty_step": 21,
  "reason": "The Orchestrator abandoned the search for the actual trench conditions and high-pressure Freon-12 density, instead instructing the Assistant to use a rough approximation. This directly led to the incorrect volume calculation of 208 mL."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "Orchestrator",
  "faulty_step": 5,
  "reason": "The Orchestrator dropped the May 2020 temporal constraint by directing WebSurfer to the current Ensembl 113 result instead of locating the dog genome release/files active in May 2020. This led directly to the incorrect final URL."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "WebSurfer",
  "faulty_step": 4,
  "reason": "WebSurfer returned a raw, unsummarized search-results page with metadata and OCR instead of extracting the needed precipitation data. That content triggered the Orchestrator's content-filter error and crashed the run."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "WebSurfer",
  "faulty_step": 8,
  "reason": "WebSurfer only opened the BASE homepage and did not perform the required DDC 633 search/browse to retrieve the 2020 language/flag data, so the task remained unresolved and the run aborted."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "WebSurfer",
  "faulty_step": 16,
  "reason": "WebSurfer typed the origin but failed to select a specific address from the FedEx autocomplete, leaving the rate calculator incomplete. This caused the repeated CONTINUE stalls and prevented the run from obtaining a usable quote before max rounds."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "WebSurfer",
  "faulty_step": 12,
  "reason": "WebSurfer ignored the instruction to switch to TimeAndDate and continued interacting with Weather Underground, starting a loop that consumed the time budget. Accessing TimeAndDate at that point would likely have allowed the needed June temperature data to be retrieved and the task completed."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "WebSurfer",
  "faulty_step": 4,
  "reason": "WebSurfer accepted unfiltered Bing search results as gyms within 200m without verifying distances, so far-away gyms like Equinox Flatiron remained in the candidate set and the final answer was wrong."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "WebSurfer",
  "faulty_step": 12,
  "reason": "WebSurfer was instructed to explore the USGS species profile but only clicked a control and returned the top of the page, failing to scroll to the Nonindigenous Occurrences section where the year appears. If it had scrolled and extracted that section, the run would most likely have succeeded."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "Orchestrator",
  "faulty_step": 92,
  "reason": "The Orchestrator's ledger update after WebSurfer's step triggered an unrecovered Azure content-filter error, preventing a clean final answer. This is the decisive failure point."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "WebSurfer",
  "faulty_step": 89,
  "reason": "WebSurfer entered 'monday.com' into the Reporting File Number field instead of the Company Name field, causing an invalid SEC-EDGAR search and preventing retrieval of the IPO filing/executive list. Correcting this step would likely have allowed the system to find the historical C-suite and answer correctly."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "Orchestrator",
  "faulty_step": 31,
  "reason": "The Orchestrator's replan treated a single blog's list of kid-friendly hikes as sufficient and moved directly to TripAdvisor rating checks, abandoning the requirement to verify that each hike was recommended by at least three different people with kids."
}
